   "gap": "Merin's definitions and complete argument are not all reconstructed on the routed text: (a) Definition 8(a) requires the value range of a relevance measure to be a subinterval, proper or improper, of the extended reals (p. 269); rationality-4-3 lines 172-180 state the joint-table dependence and differentiability but not this interval clause. (b) Definition 9 states that ordinal equivalence holds iff T' = f(T) for some isotonic f (p. 270, n. 9); rationality-4-3 lines 291-293 give only the direction that increasing transforms preserve rankings, and the converse is neither stated nor proved. (c) The p. 268 claim that, for mutually relevant A and B, A can be more relevant to B than B to A under one measure, less under another and equally under a third, is not realized by a model; the routed D and L direction comparisons (rationality-4-3 lines 235-245) run the same way. (d) The p. 272 general claim that any relevance measure affords some conditional homomorphisms is not stated or shown.",
