   "gap": "Merin's raven example is not presented as the source states it (p. 272): the predicament (1) H supported by A=A1A2, (2) the logical equivalent G supported by B=B1B2, (3) the white-shoe embellishment, and the deductivist criterion that logical equivalents be treated alike for support, which is what makes B's support of H paradoxical; rationality-4-3 lines 398-425 give the solution model but not the predicament and criterion. The routed classification of the chapter's claims by kind (w02b-p15-024 lines 37-61, 'three' empirical claims) does not classify every non-formal claim of the chapter, e.g. the Mercury judgment report (p. 268), the Linda response report and the delta-p evidence report (p. 273), and the popularity of relevance theory in linguistics (p. 273).",
